   "evidence": "Lines 84-86: the H\u00f6lder half is `(HolderOnWith.sum fun l _ \u21a6 (A l).holderOnWith_iteratedFDeriv_comp_left hs (hg l) (hb l).2).congr \u2026`, which never uses `(hb l).1`. Lines 87-91: the norm half uses only `(hb l).1`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Holder/CompLinear.lean",
   "fix": "Split it into `ContinuousLinearMap.holderOnWith_iteratedFDeriv_sum_comp_left` (hypotheses `hs`, `hg`, `\u2200 l, HolderOnWith (C l) \u03b1 \u2026`; constant `\u2211 \u2016A l\u2016\u208a * C l`) and `ContinuousLinearMap.norm_iteratedFDeriv_sum_comp_left_le` (hypotheses `hs`, `hg`, `\u2200 l, \u2200 z \u2208 s, \u2016\u2026\u2016 \u2264 M l`). Use both in the disc theorem.",
   "issue": "`norm_iteratedFDeriv_sum_comp_left_le_and_holderOnWith` takes `hb : \u2200 l, (norm bound by M l) \u2227 HolderOnWith (M l) \u2026` and returns a conjunction. The H\u00f6lder conclusion needs only `(hb l).2`, but callers must still prove the norm bound, and both bounds must share the single constant `M l`. This makes the general public lemma less reusable than it should be.",
